{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790984978,"nonce":"bYsk0xsHqxMR2BbS9mCGxoY+nD8=","message":"Scope, surveyed 2026-10-03: more than caribou_abi.\n- caribou_abi: Enum\u003cT\u003e is #[repr(transparent)] over *const EnumData, so Option\u003cEnum\u003cT\u003e\u003e has no niche and is not FFI-safe. Either Enum\u003cT\u003e wraps NonNull\u003cEnumData\u003e (Option then crosses as a nullable pointer), or a separate optional-enum carrier.\n- The argument must be marked nullable in the plugin table and in its interface: caribou-plugin's interfaces() types an ENUM parameter as TypeRef::Enum, with no nullable form. TypeRef::Enum is read in caribou/src/data.rs and link.rs, caribou-ash, and caribou-python.\n- Each frontend's conversion must pass null through: caribou-ash's enum_from_haxe (proto.rs, link.rs), caribou-runtime's caribou_plugin_enum_from_haxe (AOT, via caribou-driver's aot.rs), Python, and Wren and Zyntax through TypeRef.\nNo current consumer: xwindow declares setTheme(Option\u003cEnum\u003cTheme\u003e\u003e), but cb_window has not moved onto xwindow yet.","files":null}]}